{"seconds": 33.0, "exit": 0, "final": "Perfect! **Nxe7** is the best move. It leads to a forced win:\n- **1. Nxe7** removes the defender of the knight\n- **1...Rxe7** (best try) and **2. Qxf6** wins the knight with a devastating position\n- If Black captures with **2...Rxf5**, White has **3. Qh8#** checkmate!\n\n---\n\n## Coaching Note\n\n**You missed a pin and deflection tactic.** When a piece is pinned (the Black knight on f6 couldn't move without exposing the bishop), attacking its only defender can be devastating. Here, removing the bishop with Nxe7 forces the rook to recapture, leaving the pinned knight undefended. Then Qxf6 wins cleanly with checkmate threats. Always look for ways to eliminate defenders of pinned pieces\u2014it's one of the most common winning patterns at every level.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nxe7\", \"line\": [\"Nxe7\", \"Rxe7\", \"Qxf6\", \"Rxf5\", \"Qh8#\"], \"motifs\": [\"pin\", \"deflection\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/pp2bp1p/3p1n2/2rN1RQ1/8/1P4P1/P6P/3R3K w - - 8 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/pp2bp1p/3p1n2/2rN1RQ1/8/1P4P1/P6P/3R3K w - - 8 27"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/pp2bp1p/3p1n2/2rN1RQ1/8/1P4P1/P6P/3R3K w - - 8 27", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/pp2bp1p/3p1n2/2rN1RQ1/8/1P4P1/P6P/3R3K w - - 8 27", "square": "f5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/pp2bp1p/3p1n2/2rN1RQ1/8/1P4P1/P6P/3R3K w - - 8 27", "square": "d5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/pp2bp1p/3p1n2/2rN1RQ1/8/1P4P1/P6P/3R3K w - - 8 27", "square": "d1"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/pp2bp1p/3p1n2/2rN1RQ1/8/1P4P1/P6P/3R3K w - - 8 27", "square": "f6"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "3qrk2/pp2bp1p/3p1n2/2rN1RQ1/8/1P4P1/P6P/3R3K w - - 8 27", "square": "e7"}}, {"tool": "chess